 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**How `request`, `session` and `g` reach every template**\n\n- **`g` and `request`** are injected per render. `render_template` → `_render` (`src/tessel/templating.py:123`) calls `app.fill_template_scope()` (`src/tessel/app.py:588`). That runs the registered context injectors, starting with `_base_template_vars()` (`src/tessel/templating.py:21`), which puts `g` and, inside a request, `request` into the template context. It is registered as the default injector in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:182-184`.\n- **`session`** is not in the per-render dict. The Jinja environment gets `request`, `session` and `g` as globals in `create_jinja_environment` (`src/tessel/app.py:493-503`), so they are available even in imported templates. `session` is the `LocalProxy` from `src/tessel/globals.py:60`, and `_base_template_vars` skips it deliberately (comment at `templating.py:30`).\n- The proxies themselves are defined in `src/tessel/globals.py:40-61`, backed by the `app_ctx` ContextVar.\n\n**Adding your own variables**\n\n- **Per-render values:** decorate a function with `@app.ctx_injector` (`src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:550`). It returns a dict that is merged into the context for every template. Values passed to `render_template(**kwargs)` take precedence over injected ones (`src/tessel/app.py:607-616`).\n- **Bundle-scoped:** `@bp.ctx_injector` applies only to templates rendered from that bundle's views. `@bp.app_ctx_injector` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:644`) applies to every template in the app.\n- **Plain functions or constants as globals:** `@app.template_global()` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:780`) or `app.add_template_global(f, name=...)` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:811`), which write to `jinja_env.globals`. Bundles have the equivalent `@bp.app_template_global` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:558`).",
